{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_142748_32b188", "exit_code": 0, "text": "**Q1. If I buy the base model with 32 GB of memory, can I upgrade to 128 GB myself later?**\nYes. The Aurora 14 supports up to 128 GB, and customers may upgrade memory themselves. Upgrading does not void the warranty when using qualified modules from the Aurora compatibility list.\n*Citation: Section 2: Memory and Storage Upgrades*\n\n**Q2. What warranty comes standard, and can I extend it?**\nThe Aurora 14 includes a 3-year on-site, next-business-day warranty. You can extend coverage to 4 or 5 years at purchase or within 90 days of purchase.\n*Citation: Section 1: Warranty and Support*\n\n**Q3. How many external monitors can I run from one dock?**\nThrough a single Thunderbolt 5 dock, the Aurora 14 supports up to three external 4K displays at 60 Hz, or two external displays at up to 8K 60 Hz.\n*Citation: Section 3: Docking and External Displays*\n\n**Q4. What happens if the BIOS is attacked?**\nThe system's self-healing BIOS continuously checks firmware integrity. If the BIOS is corrupted or attacked, the system automatically restores a protected copy at the next boot.\n*Citation: Section 4: Security Features*\n\n**Q5. Is Aurora 14 certified for Ubuntu 24.04?**\nNot covered in the provided documentation. You should contact your sales representative or the technical support team to confirm OS certification details.", "tokens": {"input": 4394, "output": 332, "total": 4726, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 6448, "timestamp": 1790803676086}